{#
    One picture in a fill page's image picker — the gallery modal's tile 1:1
    (square thumb + `_gallery_asset_caption`: file name, pixel size, format),
    so a picture reads the same in the picker as in the gallery.

    The grid CELL is the fill-gallery `thumb` target (the folder filter hides
    cells, not buttons); the inner button carries the host page's own pick
    wiring, passed in as `attrs`.

    Vars: asset (url, directoryId, tooltip, uploadedAt + caption fields),
          attrs (hash of extra button attributes), class (extra button classes).
    Without `asset` it renders the NEW-UPLOAD tile for the picker's
    <template>: fill-gallery replaces the __KEY__ placeholders with the
    upload response (id, url, caption) — keep the two lists in sync.
#}
{% set asset = asset ?? {
    url: '__URL__',
    directoryId: '',
    tooltip: '__TOOLTIP__',
    uploadedAt: '__UPLOADED_AT__',
    name: '__NAME__',
    nameBase: '__NAME_BASE__',
    nameExt: '__NAME_EXT__',
    sizeLabel: '__SIZE__',
    format: '__FORMAT__',
} %}
<div class="fi-gcell" data-fill-gallery-target="thumb" data-directory-id="{{ asset.directoryId ?? '' }}">
    <div class="gallery-asset fi-gt">
        <button
            type="button"
            class="gallery-asset__select fi-gsel {{ class|default('') }}"
            title="{{ asset.tooltip }} · Nahráno {{ asset.uploadedAt }}"
            {% for name, value in attrs %}{{ name }}="{{ value }}" {% endfor %}
        >
            <span class="fi-gi">
                <img
                    crossorigin="anonymous"
                    src="{{ asset.url }}"
                    alt=""
                    loading="lazy"
                >
            </span>
            {{ include('_gallery_asset_caption.html.twig', {asset: asset}) }}
        </button>
    </div>
</div>
